(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "direct continuation of ADR-2607101700 (Phase 0a rotation-gauge sector + gauge fix);\n    covers 4 more merged PRs from a self-paced /loop generate->verify->adversarially-\n    review->fix cycle run 2026-07-09" "kotoba-lang/standard-model#3 merged as 9689fb877a961611a44d171b6614e45ca2f9c163:\n    Phase 0b -- position gauge field h_mu (4x4 real matrix, row mu = physical\n    four-vector h_mu) and derived metric g_munu=h_mu.h_nu via kotoba.sm.tensor/dot\n    unmodified; flat-limit check is EXACT integer equality against\n    kotoba.sm.tensor/metric, not epsilon-close; consistency with pre-existing\n    global SO(3,1)+ (kotoba.sm.vector-field boosts/rotations) proven algebraically\n    (Lambda^T eta Lambda=eta => Lambda eta Lambda^T=eta) and checked against 7\n    concrete transformations. No general matrix inverse implemented (deferred)." "kotoba-lang/standard-model#4 merged as cc10dcb6a571451f20a5f328b7ca9d7aff0d8d62:\n    test-only edge-case coverage hardening (generator antisymmetry, field-strength\n    antisymmetry, covariant-derivative linearity, diagonal-Gram guards,\n    derived-metric symmetry) that SURFACED A REAL BUG: kotoba.sm.gauge/field-strength's\n    self-interaction term g*f^abc*A_mu^b*A_nu^c is antisymmetric under mu<->nu only\n    when excited gauge-field components share the same trace-Gram sign -- true\n    automatically for compact SU(2)/SU(3) (uniform K=1/2) but false for so(1,3)'s\n    mixed boost(-1)/rotation(+1) components. Recorded honestly as a passing test\n    documenting current (broken) behavior per this repo's practice, not silently\n    patched; fix filed as separate follow-up rather than rushed inline." "kotoba-lang/standard-model#5 merged as 9e94650961ef1792a46c77a3fb8bc307b29f64db:\n    Phase 0c -- curvature-quadratic-invariant, I = sum_k K[k][k]*(R_munu^k R^munu_k),\n    built from Phase 0a's R_munu alone, scoped to h=position-gauge-identity only\n    (the one case needing no matrix inverse). Explicitly documented as NOT the LDG\n    curvature scalar R=h^mu^h^nu.R(hbar_nu,hbar_mu) (that is LINEAR in R_munu; this\n    is QUADRATIC, same relationship Kretschmann scalar has to Riemann tensor in GR).\n    Implementing agent declined to guess at the true linear contraction's index-\n    pairing convention without an independent literature value to check against --\n    filed as named follow-up (Phase 0d) rather than risking a silently-wrong result.\n    Not guaranteed non-negative (K is indefinite)." "independent adversarial review (a dedicated task, no code changed, not itself a\n    PR): re-derived so(1,3) commutation relations, Gram-matrix signs (boost=-1,\n    rotation=+1, verified by hand from Dirac-representation gamma matrices), and the\n    generalized structure-constant formula from Peskin&Schroeder BEFORE reading the\n    implementation, then checked for divergence -- found existing algebra correct,\n    but identified the EXACT root cause of PR #4's antisymmetry bug: self-interaction-term\n    indexed structure-constants as f-abc[a][b][c] (output index FIRST) where\n    structure-constants' own definition [T_A,T_B]=if^ABD*T_D puts the output/target\n    index THIRD; verified the fix (swap to f-abc[b][c][a]) three independent ways\n    (re-indexed reimplementation, direct matrix ground truth via -ig[A_0,A_1],\n    bit-identical SU(2) regression) before any production code touched" "kotoba-lang/standard-model#6 merged as 6ed2ca0d9a881d8a8126328001dabb2bc394ff2a:\n    implements exactly the review's diagnosed fix (get-in f-abc [a b cc] ->\n    [b cc a]); SU(2)/SU(3) proven bit-identical via independent-oracle regression\n    test; so(1,3) antisymmetry recovery proven via PR #4's own counterexample\n    flipping from equal (+0.35/+0.35, broken) to negated (-0.35/+0.35, correct)\n    plus 3 additional mixed boost/rotation excitation patterns" "test suite grew 22 tests/85 assertions (ADR-2607051500 original) -> 30/428\n    (Phase 0a, ADR-2607101700) -> 47 tests/2065 assertions (end of this pass),\n    CI green (JDK 17+21) at every merged step, zero regressions" "superproject manifest/west.yml pin advanced through each merge via sanctioned\n    GitHub API single-entry commit path; final state\n    6ed2ca0d9a881d8a8126328001dabb2bc394ff2a, superproject commit\n    b4300522aa098f8d0d963e1542c201e114441483" "explicitly out of scope, deferred (extends not replaces ADR-2607101700 boundary):\n    general (non-identity) h_mu / reciprocal frame h-bar (needs matrix inverse, not\n    implemented anywhere in this codebase), the true linear LDG curvature scalar\n    (needs matrix inverse + literature-verified index-pairing convention),\n    Einstein multivector, GTG action/field equations, GR-equivalence proof,\n    dark-matter/dark-energy/de-Sitter extension, combined h_mu+Omega_mu covariant\n    derivative, quantization/RGE/scattering/lattice (unchanged from ADR-2607051500)" "does not claim gravity or unification is implemented -- the review-finds-a-real-\n    bug-in-already-merged-code outcome is the intended product of investing in\n    adversarial test coverage and independent review, not a failure of the earlier\n    passes")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607101700" "adr-2607051500")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607101900-kotoba-lang-standard-model-gtg-position-gauge-and-antisymmetry-fix"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-09"), (:adr/body "see 2607101900-kotoba-lang-standard-model-gtg-position-gauge-and-antisymmetry-fix.edn"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-09"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607101900: kotoba-lang/standard-model — GTG position-gauge sector (Phase 0b), curvature quadratic invariant (Phase 0c), and a field-strength antisymmetry fix found by an independent review loop"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))